["<aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout why\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>The SKS (Simonov self loading carbine) has a huge market of add ons. A few of them turn a legal rifle into a restricted or prohibited one, and that is a crime.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three columns. GO, green: sling, recoil pad, fixed stock, soft point ammunition. ASK a gunsmith, orange: scope mount, a stock swap, trigger work, removing the bayonet. NO, red: cutting the barrel, unpinning the magazine, a bullpup stock, a suppressor.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Upgrades: go, ask, no</text>\n<rect x=\"10.0\" y=\"46.0\" width=\"124.0\" height=\"216.0\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#2E7D4F\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"10.0\" y=\"46.0\" width=\"124.0\" height=\"34.0\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2E7D4F\" stroke=\"#2E7D4F\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"72.0\" y=\"70.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">GO</text><text x=\"72.0\" y=\"110.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sling</text><text x=\"72.0\" y=\"148.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Recoil pad</text><text x=\"72.0\" y=\"186.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fixed stock</text><text x=\"72.0\" y=\"224.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Soft points</text><rect x=\"138.0\" y=\"46.0\" width=\"124.0\" height=\"216.0\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"138.0\" y=\"46.0\" width=\"124.0\" height=\"34.0\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"70.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">ASK</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"110.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Scope mount</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"148.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stock swap</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"186.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Trigger work</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"224.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bayonet off</text><rect x=\"266.0\" y=\"46.0\" width=\"124.0\" height=\"216.0\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#B3261E\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><rect x=\"266.0\" y=\"46.0\" width=\"124.0\" height=\"34.0\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#B3261E\" stroke=\"#B3261E\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"328.0\" y=\"70.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">NO</text><text x=\"328.0\" y=\"110.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cut barrel</text><text x=\"328.0\" y=\"148.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Unpin mag</text><text x=\"328.0\" y=\"186.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bullpup</text><text x=\"328.0\" y=\"224.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Suppressor</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"288.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">ASK means a qualified gunsmith.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Green: change freely. Orange: ask a qualified gunsmith first. Red: never (Tip on the sorting; each red item is law below).</li><li>Never alter the rifle in a way that changes its legal class.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how to read this chapter</summary><ul><li>Class depends on the Criminal Code s. 84(1) definitions and the prohibited list in SOR/98-462 (99%, read directly, both current to 30 September 2026).</li><li>The RCMP Firearms Reference Table (FRT) applies those rules to each model. It says it \"is not a legal instrument\"; the Act and Regulations are the authority (99%, FRT disclaimer).</li><li>When in doubt: a qualified gunsmith, or the RCMP Canadian Firearms Program, before you buy the part (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Barrel lengths from the RCMP reference table for Type 56 SKS records: standard 520 mm non restricted; 478 mm non restricted; 419 mm restricted; a 400 mm cut barrel prohibited. A dashed line marks 470 mm, the restricted line for semi automatic centrefire rifles.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Barrel length decides the class</text>\n<rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"66.0\" width=\"218.4\" height=\"16.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"246.4\" y=\"79.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">520 mm standard</text><text x=\"20.0\" y=\"100.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2E7D4F\" text-anchor=\"start\">Non restricted</text><rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"112.0\" width=\"200.8\" height=\"16.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"228.8\" y=\"125.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">478 mm</text><text x=\"20.0\" y=\"146.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2E7D4F\" text-anchor=\"start\">Non restricted</text><rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"158.0\" width=\"176.0\" height=\"16.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"204.0\" y=\"171.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">419 mm</text><text x=\"20.0\" y=\"192.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"start\">Restricted</text><rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"204.0\" width=\"168.0\" height=\"16.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#B3261E\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"196.0\" y=\"217.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">400 mm cut</text><text x=\"20.0\" y=\"238.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#B3261E\" text-anchor=\"start\">Prohibited</text><line x1=\"217.4\" y1=\"56.0\" x2=\"217.4\" y2=\"250.0\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><text x=\"217.4\" y=\"266.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">470 mm line</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"288.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Never cut the barrel.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Standard 520 mm barrel: non restricted <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Shortened SKS records in the FRT are restricted, or prohibited when cut <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the law and the FRT records</summary><aside class=\"callout law\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Criminal Code s. 84(1), \"restricted firearm\", paragraph (b)</div><p>\"a firearm that (i) is not a prohibited firearm, (ii) has a barrel less than 470 mm in length, and (iii) is capable of discharging centre-fire ammunition in a semi-automatic manner\"</p></aside><aside class=\"callout law\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Criminal Code s. 84(1), \"prohibited firearm\", paragraph (b)</div><p>\"a firearm that is adapted from a rifle or shotgun, whether by sawing, cutting or any other alteration, and that, as so adapted, (i) is less than 660 mm in length, or (ii) is 660 mm or greater in length and has a barrel less than 457 mm in length\"</p></aside><ul><li>FRT Type 56 SKS records (99%, read directly, valid 19 October 2026):<ul><li>520 mm: non restricted (FRN 142679, 141924, 142871, 33820).</li><li>478 mm and 483 mm: non restricted (FRN 181122, 2387).</li><li>408 mm, 419 mm, 422 mm: restricted under s. 84(1) \"restricted firearm\" para. (b) (FRN 177622, 2387, 127793).</li><li>400 mm, cut down: prohibited under s. 84(1) \"prohibited firearm\" para. (b)(ii) (FRN 2387).</li></ul></li><li>A muzzle brake does not count toward barrel length: barrel length excludes \"any component, part or accessory designed or intended to suppress the muzzle flash or reduce recoil\" (99%, s. 84(2)).</li><li>Never cut, thread or shorten the barrel (99% on the law; the advice is a Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A magazine box holding 5 rounds with a pin or rivet, in orange, that blocks more. Text: 5 rounds maximum for a semi automatic centrefire rifle magazine. Removing the pin makes it a prohibited device, a crime.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The 5 round magazine law</text>\n<rect x=\"70.0\" y=\"70.0\" width=\"120.0\" height=\"150.0\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"82.0\" y=\"82.4\" width=\"65.3\" height=\"19.2\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"#C9A227\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"85.0\" y1=\"82.4\" x2=\"85.0\" y2=\"101.6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M147.3 83.9 Q173.2 86.2 178.0 92.0 Q173.2 97.8 147.3 100.1 Z\" fill=\"#B87333\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M168.4 88.5 Q177.0 92.0 168.4 95.5\" fill=\"#9AA0A6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"82.0\" y=\"100.4\" width=\"65.3\" height=\"19.2\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"#C9A227\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"85.0\" y1=\"100.4\" x2=\"85.0\" y2=\"119.6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M147.3 101.9 Q173.2 104.2 178.0 110.0 Q173.2 115.8 147.3 118.1 Z\" fill=\"#B87333\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M168.4 106.5 Q177.0 110.0 168.4 113.5\" fill=\"#9AA0A6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"82.0\" y=\"118.4\" width=\"65.3\" height=\"19.2\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"#C9A227\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"85.0\" y1=\"118.4\" x2=\"85.0\" y2=\"137.6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M147.3 119.9 Q173.2 122.2 178.0 128.0 Q173.2 133.8 147.3 136.1 Z\" fill=\"#B87333\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M168.4 124.5 Q177.0 128.0 168.4 131.5\" fill=\"#9AA0A6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"82.0\" y=\"136.4\" width=\"65.3\" height=\"19.2\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"#C9A227\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"85.0\" y1=\"136.4\" x2=\"85.0\" y2=\"155.6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M147.3 137.9 Q173.2 140.2 178.0 146.0 Q173.2 151.8 147.3 154.1 Z\" fill=\"#B87333\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M168.4 142.5 Q177.0 146.0 168.4 149.5\" fill=\"#9AA0A6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"82.0\" y=\"154.4\" width=\"65.3\" height=\"19.2\" rx=\"1.5\" fill=\"#C9A227\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"85.0\" y1=\"154.4\" x2=\"85.0\" y2=\"173.6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M147.3 155.9 Q173.2 158.2 178.0 164.0 Q173.2 169.8 147.3 172.1 Z\" fill=\"#B87333\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M168.4 160.5 Q177.0 164.0 168.4 167.5\" fill=\"#9AA0A6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><rect x=\"70.0\" y=\"186.0\" width=\"120.0\" height=\"10.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"130.0\" cy=\"191.0\" r=\"6.0\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"130.0\" y=\"244.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pin or rivet</text><text x=\"214.0\" y=\"90.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">5 rounds max for a</text><text x=\"214.0\" y=\"110.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">semi auto centrefire</text><text x=\"214.0\" y=\"130.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">rifle magazine.</text><text x=\"214.0\" y=\"164.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#B3261E\" text-anchor=\"start\">Removing the pin</text><text x=\"214.0\" y=\"184.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#B3261E\" text-anchor=\"start\">makes it a prohibited</text><text x=\"214.0\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#B3261E\" text-anchor=\"start\">device. A crime.</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"288.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">SOR/98-462 Part 4. Criminal Code s. 84.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>5 rounds max in a magazine made for a semi automatic centrefire long gun <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Never remove or defeat the pin or rivet <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the law in full</summary><aside class=\"callout law\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">SOR/98-462, Schedule, Part 4, item 3(1)(a)</div><p>A cartridge magazine is prohibited if it is \"capable of containing more than five cartridges of the type for which the magazine was originally designed\" and made for \"a semi-automatic firearm other than a semi-automatic handgun\".</p></aside><ul><li>A larger magazine is legal only if altered so the change \"cannot be easily removed\" and it \"cannot be easily further altered\" (99%, item 3(4)). Approved methods include a plug, sleeve, rod, pin or flange fixed by \"welding, brazing or any other similar method\" in a steel casing (99%, item 3(5)).</li><li>RCMP: possession is legal if the magazine \"has been permanently altered so that it cannot hold more than the number of cartridges allowed by law\" (95%, RCMP page modified 18 October 2024).</li><li>Since Bill C-21 (December 2023): \"it is a Criminal Code offence to alter or modify a cartridge magazine to hold more than its lawful capacity\", and \"individuals require a valid firearms licence to acquire a cartridge magazine\" (95%, RCMP).</li><li>\"Cartridge magazine means a device or container from which ammunition may be fed into the firing chamber of a firearm\" (99%, s. 84(1)). So the fixed SKS magazine counts (90%, my reading).</li><li>Capacity is counted in the cartridge the magazine was designed for (95%, RCMP).</li><li>Aftermarket detachable magazine conversions: the FRT notes the SKS D \"can use any magazine intended for use with the Kalashnikov AK design. As such higher capacity magazines will be encountered\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Any magazine you use must be a legal 5 round one <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Changing your rifle to take detachable magazines: ask a gunsmith first (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Overall length bars: the standard SKS is about 1020 mm. A folding or telescoping stock that lets it fire when shorter than 660 mm makes it restricted. A bullpup stock is a prohibited device.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stocks: the 660 mm line</text>\n<line x1=\"20.0\" y1=\"120.0\" x2=\"380.0\" y2=\"120.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"100.0\" width=\"357.0\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#D9DCD7\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"125.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Standard: about 1020 mm</text><rect x=\"20.0\" y=\"170.0\" width=\"210.0\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#F3D1C4\" stroke=\"#B3261E\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"125.0\" y=\"195.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#B3261E\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Folded under 660</text><line x1=\"251.0\" y1=\"86.0\" x2=\"251.0\" y2=\"222.0\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><text x=\"257.0\" y=\"82.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"start\">660 mm</text><text x=\"30.0\" y=\"252.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#B3261E\" text-anchor=\"start\">Fires when folded under 660 mm: restricted.</text><text x=\"30.0\" y=\"274.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#B3261E\" text-anchor=\"start\">Bullpup stock: prohibited device.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>A stock that lets it fire when folded under 660 mm: restricted <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>A bullpup stock: a prohibited device <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: stocks and the law</summary><aside class=\"callout law\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Criminal Code s. 84(1), \"restricted firearm\", paragraph (c)</div><p>\"a firearm that is designed or adapted to be fired when reduced to a length of less than 660 mm by folding, telescoping or otherwise\"</p></aside><ul><li>Bullpup stock: a prohibited device, \"a stock that, when combined with a firearm, reduces the overall length of the firearm such that a substantial part of the reloading action or the magazine-well is located behind the trigger of the firearm when it is held in the normal firing position\" (99%, SOR/98-462 Part 4 item 2).</li><li>The FRT notes \"a large number of aftermarket accessories, including scopes and mounts, thumbhole stocks, peep sights\" on non restricted Type 56 SKS records <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. A fixed replacement stock that keeps the length is common (85%, my reading). Folding, telescoping or bullpup: ask a gunsmith and check the law first (Tip).</li><li>Keep the original stock. It holds value and is always legal on your rifle (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Never: full auto or bump fire parts; a trigger device for rapid fire; a suppressor; cutting the barrel short; a magazine over 5 rounds; a bullpup stock.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Never do these</text>\n<circle cx=\"32.0\" cy=\"60.0\" r=\"9.9\" fill=\"#B3261E\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"27.9\" y1=\"56.0\" x2=\"36.0\" y2=\"64.0\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"36.0\" y1=\"56.0\" x2=\"27.9\" y2=\"64.0\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"54.0\" y=\"65.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Full auto or bump fire parts</text><circle cx=\"32.0\" cy=\"94.0\" r=\"9.9\" fill=\"#B3261E\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"27.9\" y1=\"90.0\" x2=\"36.0\" y2=\"98.0\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"36.0\" y1=\"90.0\" x2=\"27.9\" y2=\"98.0\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"54.0\" y=\"99.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Trigger device for rapid fire</text><circle cx=\"32.0\" cy=\"128.0\" r=\"9.9\" fill=\"#B3261E\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"27.9\" y1=\"124.0\" x2=\"36.0\" y2=\"132.1\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"36.0\" y1=\"124.0\" x2=\"27.9\" y2=\"132.1\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"54.0\" y=\"133.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Suppressor (silencer)</text><circle cx=\"32.0\" cy=\"162.0\" r=\"9.9\" fill=\"#B3261E\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"27.9\" y1=\"157.9\" x2=\"36.0\" y2=\"166.1\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"36.0\" y1=\"157.9\" x2=\"27.9\" y2=\"166.1\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"54.0\" y=\"167.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Barrel cut short</text><circle cx=\"32.0\" cy=\"196.0\" r=\"9.9\" fill=\"#B3261E\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"27.9\" y1=\"191.9\" x2=\"36.0\" y2=\"200.1\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"36.0\" y1=\"191.9\" x2=\"27.9\" y2=\"200.1\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"54.0\" y=\"201.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Magazine over 5 rounds</text><circle cx=\"32.0\" cy=\"230.0\" r=\"9.9\" fill=\"#B3261E\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"27.9\" y1=\"225.9\" x2=\"36.0\" y2=\"234.1\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"36.0\" y1=\"225.9\" x2=\"27.9\" y2=\"234.1\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"54.0\" y=\"235.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Bullpup stock</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"288.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Each makes it restricted or prohibited.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Full auto, rapid fire triggers, suppressors: prohibited <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Each one is a crime, not a gun shop choice <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the law behind each red item</summary><ul><li>Automatic: an \"automatic firearm\" is one capable of \"discharging projectiles in rapid succession during one pressure of the trigger\". It is a prohibited firearm (99%, Criminal Code s. 84(1)).</li><li>Trigger devices: \"Any electrical or mechanical device that is designed or adapted to operate the trigger mechanism of a semi-automatic firearm for the purpose of causing the firearm to discharge cartridges in rapid succession\" is a prohibited device (99%, SOR/98-462 Part 4 item 1).</li><li>Suppressor: \"a device or contrivance designed or intended to muffle or stop the sound or report of a firearm\" is a prohibited device (99%, s. 84(1)).</li><li>A slam fire or a rifle that doubles is a fault, not a feature: stop and see a gunsmith (Tip; chapter 1).</li><li>Bayonet: the law texts read for this course do not name bayonets (85%, my reading). Folding it away is the norm; removing it is a gunsmith job and it should not be on the rifle when hunting (Tip). <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> with the RCMP if you plan to remove or replace it.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 290\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Upgrade order as steps: 1 gunsmith check first, 2 soft point hunting ammunition, 3 a good sling, 4 better sights after asking a gunsmith, 5 practice ammunition.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"290\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Money order (Tip)</text>\n<rect x=\"14.0\" y=\"220.0\" width=\"70.0\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"49.0\" y=\"242.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><rect x=\"88.0\" y=\"186.0\" width=\"70.0\" height=\"74.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"123.0\" y=\"208.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text><rect x=\"162.0\" y=\"152.0\" width=\"70.0\" height=\"108.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"197.0\" y=\"174.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><rect x=\"236.0\" y=\"118.0\" width=\"70.0\" height=\"142.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"271.0\" y=\"140.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><rect x=\"310.0\" y=\"84.0\" width=\"70.0\" height=\"176.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"345.0\" y=\"106.0\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5</text><circle cx=\"25.0\" cy=\"56.0\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"25.0\" y=\"61.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><text x=\"41.0\" y=\"61.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Gunsmith check first</text><circle cx=\"25.0\" cy=\"77.0\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"25.0\" y=\"82.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text><text x=\"41.0\" y=\"82.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Soft point hunting ammo</text><circle cx=\"25.0\" cy=\"98.0\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"25.0\" y=\"103.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><text x=\"41.0\" y=\"103.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">A good sling</text><circle cx=\"25.0\" cy=\"119.0\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"25.0\" y=\"124.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><text x=\"41.0\" y=\"124.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Better sights (ask)</text><circle cx=\"25.0\" cy=\"140.0\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"25.0\" y=\"145.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5</text><text x=\"41.0\" y=\"145.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Practice ammunition</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>1: gunsmith check. 2: soft point ammunition. 3: sling (Tip).</li><li>Then sights, and lots of practice (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: upgrades in order, with notes</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Upgrade</th><th>Why</th><th>Note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Gunsmith inspection</td><td>Headspace, pin, bore</td><td>Price <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> locally</td></tr><tr><td>Soft point ammunition</td><td>Legal for deer</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-sks-07/4\">Chapter 7</a> prices</td></tr><tr><td>Sling</td><td>Hands free carry</td><td>Uses the existing sling mounts (99%, FRT)</td></tr><tr><td>Recoil pad</td><td>Comfort</td><td>Slip on, no change to the rifle (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>Peep sight or scope mount</td><td>Better aiming</td><td>Top cover mounts can shift zero (Tip). Ask a gunsmith</td></tr><tr><td>Practice ammunition</td><td>The real upgrade</td><td>Corrosive? <a href=\"#/s/mc-sks-05\">Chapter 5</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Prices: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>. Not checked for this chapter. Ask two Fraser Valley shops.</li><li>Not worth it on a hunting SKS (Tip): high capacity looks, lights (illegal to hunt with, 99%), bayonet parts, bipods.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Before every season: 1 read the marks on the left side of the receiver, 2 find the record in the RCMP Firearms Reference Table, 3 read the news on the federal SKS review, 4 ask a gunsmith or the RCMP.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Check the status each season</text>\n<rect x=\"40.0\" y=\"56.0\" width=\"320.0\" height=\"42.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"62.0\" cy=\"77.0\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"62.0\" y=\"82.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><text x=\"84.0\" y=\"74.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Read the marks</text><text x=\"84.0\" y=\"92.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">left side of the receiver</text><rect x=\"40.0\" y=\"108.0\" width=\"320.0\" height=\"42.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"62.0\" cy=\"129.0\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"62.0\" y=\"134.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text><text x=\"84.0\" y=\"126.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Find the record</text><text x=\"84.0\" y=\"144.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">RCMP reference table</text><rect x=\"40.0\" y=\"160.0\" width=\"320.0\" height=\"42.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"62.0\" cy=\"181.0\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"62.0\" y=\"186.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><text x=\"84.0\" y=\"178.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Read the news</text><text x=\"84.0\" y=\"196.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">federal SKS review</text><rect x=\"40.0\" y=\"212.0\" width=\"320.0\" height=\"42.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"62.0\" cy=\"233.0\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"62.0\" y=\"238.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><text x=\"84.0\" y=\"230.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Ask</text><text x=\"84.0\" y=\"248.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">gunsmith or RCMP</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"288.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Laws change. VERIFY each season.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>The SKS is under federal review (80%, 21 October 2026).</li><li>Before each season: check the FRT and the news. <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how to check</summary><ul><li>Read the marks on the left side of the receiver: \"Type 56\" in Chinese script, an arsenal number in a triangle or rectangle, the serial number (99%, FRT notes).</li><li>Find the matching record in the RCMP <a href=\"https://rcmp.ca/en/firearms/firearms-reference-table\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Firearms Reference Table</a> under Norinco, \"Type 56 SKS\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. The PDF is very large; a gunsmith or the RCMP can look it up for you (Tip).</li><li>News: the classification review announced 5 December 2025 includes the SKS; on 21 October 2026 the advisory group had not met (80%, The Canadian Press).</li><li>If the law changes, the government publishes an order and the RCMP updates its lists. Do not guess. Ask the RCMP Canadian Firearms Program (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<aside class=\"callout rule\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): If a part changes what the rifle is, it is not an upgrade. It is a charge.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Buying a folding or bullpup stock online because \"the shop sold it\".</li><li>Prying the rivet out of the magazine \"just to clean it\".</li><li>Cutting the barrel to make a handy carbine.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Photograph the left side markings of your receiver. Bring the photo to a gunsmith with your questions list.</p></aside>","<ul><li><a href=\"https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/C-46/section-84.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Criminal Code s. 84</a>, current to 30 September 2026, last amended 18 July 2026, read 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/regulations/SOR-98-462/FullText.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOR/98-462</a>, Part 4 items 1 to 3, current to 30 September 2026, read 2026-10-23 (95 to 99%)</li><li>RCMP, <a href=\"https://rcmp.ca/en/firearms/classes-firearms/maximum-permitted-magazine-capacity\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Maximum permitted magazine capacity</a>, modified 18 October 2024 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li>RCMP, <a href=\"https://rcmp.ca/en/firearms/firearms-reference-table\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Firearms Reference Table (PDF)</a>, valid 19 October 2026, Norinco Type 56 SKS records, read directly 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li>The Canadian Press, <a href=\"https://www.cp24.com/news/canada/2026/10/21/group-assisting-canadas-long-planned-review-of-firearms-including-sks-has-yet-to-meet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">21 October 2026</a> and <a href=\"https://www.cp24.com/news/canada/2025/12/05/minister-says-government-launching-review-of-firearms-classification-regime\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">5 December 2025</a> <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li></ul>"]